dream.sh now saves its per-run spend to the audit-log branch, the same way social.sh does. Committed as b2998a11 and noted on #944. It hasn't run in production yet: dream has a 7-day cooldown, so the first real row will come with the next cycle.

What it writes: one line per dream run to phases/dream/spend.jsonl, either {ts, phase:"dream", day, exit, usage_records:[…]} or "usage":"no_terminal_emit" when the run left no usage record. A missing record is never written as zero.

Where it runs: right after report_dream_spend || true. Every exit path after the agent passes that line, and the sink finishes before the diff-scope guard and before the cleanup trap's commit and push of main. It never touches main's checkout or index. It only fetches into refs/remotes/origin/audit-log and works in a temporary worktree under ${TMPDIR:-/tmp}, which is removed afterwards. A test with uncommitted changes on main shows its status, index and HEAD are unchanged after the sink runs, so the scope guard sees nothing new. The sink always returns 0.

Differences from the social version (full list in the commit body):
• Every sink line goes to stderr with a dream: prefix, because all of dream.sh's spend output already does.
• The exit code comes from dream's exit_code variable.
• The audit-log commit message uses date for its timestamp, because dream.sh has no SESSION_TIME.
• There is one call site instead of two, because dream.sh has no early exit between the agent and the report.

Tests: I added dream sink a–g to tests/harness_logic.sh. They extract the functions from the shipped script and run against a local bare origin, with uncommitted changes on main. They cover:
• the row's contents
• two runs giving two rows
• no_terminal_emit when there is no usage record
• origin with no audit-log branch: one skip line, nothing changed
• main untouched
• a rejected push being retried
• the call sitting right after the report

I ran both positive controls one at a time, each in a single break → run → restore command:
• No-op append: dream sink a failed by name, along with the row-dependent b, c and f checks.
• Retry removed: exactly dream sink f failed.

Both passed again after restoring (272/272), and no NEUTERED marker is left in the file.

Checks: bash -n on dream.sh, the harness suite, cargo build, cargo test, clippy with -D warnings and cargo fmt --check all pass. In ARCHITECTURE.md, I corrected the line that said "dream.sh … still print only" in place, keeping the old wording as a recorded superseded claim, and added the dream.sh entry.

